=== Water Level ===
Most Plants require to be watered in order to advance to the next Growth Stage.
* The {{Blue|Water}} level can be inspected in {{green|2}} ways: ({{gray|A}}) hovering over the plant while holding any [[Hydrocan]] or ({{gray|B}}) using the {{item|Plant Diagnostics Tool}}'s {{Ability|Analyze}}.
* {{Blue|Water}} varies between {{red|-100}} and {{green|+100}} whether the plant requires to be watered:
** below {{red|0}}, there is a chance to not advance to the next Growth Stage;
** at {{red|-100}}, its growth will be halted;
** if it does not require to be watered, {{Blue|Water}} will stay at {{green|+100}}.
* When a Growth Cycle ends, the {{Blue|Water}} level decreases by {{MoreInfoNeeded|is it a % or an absolute value? Apparently, it's 2-3 Water Levels ????}} units. {{Blue|Water}} depletion is affected by the following {{aqua|Effects}}:
** amplified if the plant is affected by {{Red|Water Drain}} ({{red|+30%}} loss);
** mitigated if the plant is affected by {{green|Water Retain}} ({{green|+50%}} retention);
** mitigated if the plant is affected by {{green|Improved Water Retain}} ({{green|+100%}} retention).
* The {{Blue|Water}} level can be increased by using any of the [[Hydrocan]]s at varying flows.

